abstract: "Garcia, Bermolen, Jonckheere and Shneer (Stochastic Systems, 2026) conjectured that the exponential moment governing idealised restart from a quasi-stationary distribution (QSD) on (0, L) grows like exp((lambda*-eta)L). For Lévy processes with a Gaussian component and jumps of either sign, this candidate proves exact normalised limits of every exponential moment of the interval QSD, via exact L^-2 asymptotics of the two boundary layers of the Esscher-centred QSD. The conjecture holds up to an explicit constant C*, but its ratio-one reading fails: C* < 1 for spectrally negative processes with jumps, C* > 1 for spectrally positive ones, and C* = 0.85014864899... in the source model (interval arithmetic). Idealised QSD restart has rate ~ R* exp(-eta L) and saturates uniformly in relative error, so the linear budget regime of the source's restart theorem is B = O(exp(eta L)), not o(exp(lambda* L)). Unrefereed candidate. Original code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSES.md."
